","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a2e91d9545a9424a71a724e88f418de8baad502fb9d237c2197797b3a2fa408f","compact":"10496915b3169853c22d84f602ce2d60a54ee95620b662ad936c3b14a32c85c9","nasal":"b4d3d8aa56eedabe5a15f314072056729be5cbc0570470a3202b8b42dcdc8bde"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":7,"english":"He found an exceedingly powerful elephant belonging to the cardinal point, worshipped by deities, and Dānavas, and Rākşasas, and goblins, and birds, and Uragas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.902,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dd1bc7bdb60fb5e1c7ad70f73b2bf69463220064ccf968c500ad83360d3217af","compact":"13e1a6a91e1039f59ecb6e4d6910ae9b4ba19bbeebb9d2abbb2f53dd8713a9ad","nasal":"13e1a6a91e1039f59ecb6e4d6910ae9b4ba19bbeebb9d2abbb2f53dd8713a9ad"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":8,"english":"Having gone round him, and asked him as to his welfare, he enquired after his uncles and the stealer of the horse.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2321e874a20ceb6f7d04734c264ffd1a3962627ed423954baac821de3bec3cfe","compact":"3d46cad0b97ca67d00894b39136825d2850d11636b2e684110bf47cc2c5e6e49","nasal":"79b1501e3ee7bd327bd98f5e538aa84d841860ad487e83ebcd2006b8a34ff20d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":9,"english":"Hearing this, the mighty-minded elephant of that quarter answered, 'O son of Asamañja, having attained your object, you will speedily return with the horse.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.69,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"228f01c6911a12b983972745769e51d87ab1520d6edf30126b69d830cfa20b5a","compact":"2ff8298367493396ef9d20eb863bd9e131a4154dbc4e60b42bd01919ad437ca6","nasal":"9a0a18cc2edb9c3702a25d0121421cb016bd7739d9847fb04aaa53422e590a32"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":10,"english":"And hearing those words of his, Ansumat by turns duly asked the same question of all the elephants belonging to the cardinal points.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c6ca8dcad816648a793ad92237765829a59f9b61ad4b379c173ef8be5657560","compact":"b32d2f530e93c3ce1173ec28de3a726f490d6bb230822de45257a7daea2ee512","nasal":"b32d2f530e93c3ce1173ec28de3a726f490d6bb230822de45257a7daea2ee512"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":11,"english":"And being honoured by those guardians of the cardinal points, knowing words as well as their application in regard to time, place, and person, he was asked by them saying, 'Did you come with the horse?'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.771,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6fbcfea4459a756bce9887bd0ce7eecf58f4aa5587675cb059e69ed31feaf81f","compact":"3d10634bfa500ac2a4bb7b85947de88f6d5194d8f044bdd659dc2dc77520ab3f","nasal":"1773fecdcbd595739a4f6a9e044b0d1fc6d9a90e7ec57b1ae03ce3082a181ddc"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":12,"english":"Hearing those words of theirs, that one of fleet vigour repaired to the spot where the sons of Sagara, his uncles, had been reduced to a heap of ashes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6f97de49564391cfe1fa7c6cbe9b6c2777ffa9226c5f8dee93848b52a0bb9926","compact":"7aa003e11d71e6e9c56da581e0d41adaed00151ce9c6dedf39e0431a33327f24","nasal":"7aa003e11d71e6e9c56da581e0d41adaed00151ce9c6dedf39e0431a33327f24"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":13,"english":"And (arriving there), Asamañja's son, smitten with grief, and being exceedingly afflicted at their destruction, bewailed in heaviness of heart.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dc910c912b1f5d03d793fc9f7980318d3468549c29f99d7d1f3c3d339897f64d","compact":"80ff77cf1d202eacc4a0c188d91679e6d88e031e45a0978727229e75b01239eb","nasal":"35ec4a5b04e45a502af3a7329ef6ec83f0b22b722a1bb075d78628b180d3f82d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":14,"english":"And exercised by grief and sorrow, at foremost of men espied there the sacrificial horse straying near.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eecedcbf2b87976313bdfdd20a9918ed565ad184e8f605a8dfb351919bdd6204","compact":"6d161675ef580a984a32d2faccb0eb67b8b4be93ec8ab3ea3ca734aba62ec705","nasal":"e94c4ebe54ebdb74aceff307fa003bb622eef113df948adec2a6852744dd7f74"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":15,"english":"And desirous of offering oblations of water to those princes, that highly powerful one, in need of water, did not find any watery expanse in the neighbourhood.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.565,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"15163e47a56e8b455bb07613cc51b500c391e8881a91d9eb2aabda0eb78c34eb","compact":"5dac9f583eefe5be0ac17abad677ab79206b68b4fc88d8c3f55eb79376c01004","nasal":"5dac9f583eefe5be0ac17abad677ab79206b68b4fc88d8c3f55eb79376c01004"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":16,"english":"And it came to pass, O Rāma, that surveying wide, he descried the maternal uncle to the princes, Suparna, resembling the Wind.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"78393627d5654eb0d6e06cafe412f11c6c9041e247116a5ba2e82aeef35b213c","compact":"8b274ce9fc5cb85cb190fe32a68f907209844b6dd37ff50489994c4a4987821e","nasal":"82cbedebaa71c27c16258da536fd4341884c05a61ac0a887e8851b1c2b563f66"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":17,"english":"And thereupon Vinata's son possessed of mighty strength spoke to him, saying, 'Do not lament, O foremost of men. The destruction of these was for the welfare of all.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.927,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fc59af155a22eac6081b3ddafe1a5ef0b8b22f3df8e5dd5343abcdcb216464bd","compact":"888dab82eb18df5bc78c88a4902330791c663739c9479391547c0382d17ea6a3","nasal":"888dab82eb18df5bc78c88a4902330791c663739c9479391547c0382d17ea6a3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":18,"english":"These highly powerful ones had been consumed by the peerless Kapila, therefore, you ought not to offer water to them in consonance with social usage.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cdad7ef17954c0d14b3c4ac80d4a963354556b3555880d860993dc017c7f8ba2","compact":"20fe5f38863825bceee9aa4fb44738b09fe95a567fbcb6233f606024ff21cc34","nasal":"20fe5f38863825bceee9aa4fb44738b09fe95a567fbcb6233f606024ff21cc34"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":19,"english":"Gangā, O foremost of men, is the elder daughter of Himavat. In her (streams) do you perform the watery rites of your uncles, O mighty-armed one: let that purifier of the worlds lave these reduced to a heap of ashes. And on these ashes being watered by Gangā, dear to all, the sixty thousand sons of Sagara will repair to the celestial regions.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.45,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-19","DUTT-1-41-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"adc0e04226d8325ed754f0bab7ee4bff3566ce7693393b6067da2122a66cb3c3","compact":"cb7539855d1fb42d125b5a46f7234b7a75c5e5aedbd066865e1b8599d882a2ad","nasal":"a57418b5d79d3877e93b469b7791dac7e3a841036ab225bfc3f3a5e3582092fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":20,"english":"O mighty-armed one: let that purifier of the worlds lave these reduced to a heap of ashes. And on these ashes being watered by Gangā, dear to all, the sixty thousand sons of Sagara will repair to the celestial regions.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.719,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7b93fb25d84000331eb4e5a9811ac645938d6d892736120eb78556a78e1765e6","compact":"1c1b67e98a714e54dd9ade51ad8da7570de903579ebeb79673a00d7f2e451a3f","nasal":"b1b1fd8d8df9475426f508328764cbc644e6f865a5feeaa76b312737aff4fc82"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":21,"english":"Do you, O highly pious one, go back, taking this horse, O foremost of men; and do you complete the sacrifice of your grand-father,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.759,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5dc818822d1fafe96fa5a239b30b41e8ee285696e8d28b694af3af0c87db299c","compact":"e28ca08a1d925362b422e1a4e2d0489265ccb1ed9b0263ca1833741135a80a0d","nasal":"e28ca08a1d925362b422e1a4e2d0489265ccb1ed9b0263ca1833741135a80a0d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-40-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":40,"verse":22,"english":"O hero, Hearing Suparna's speech, the exceedingly powerful Ansumat of mighty asceticism speedily taking the horse, retraced his steps.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.933,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-41-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1040022","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"286e784a08663e789af2284d28e02c2137795d63ca498306a59d8741581ab4d5","compact":"6a6df36678b473db7ac2bd9f7c609999278a9928d006b9129fc1119e4adc23e3","nasal":"5c308ed57b62cfd73f24c65509f93cb8eab547abf99d8d0f939eec44f6e57afa